00:15:00,090 --> 00:15:01,850
KEITO: Quit moping about it.

473
00:14:59,890 --> 00:15:01,850
SIGN: Currently in 5th
Rintaro Kai

474
00:15:01,850 --> 00:15:04,930
KEITO: They said there'd be bonus points 
depending on how we ranked

475
00:15:04,930 --> 00:15:06,610
KEITO: in today's competition, remember?

476
00:15:05,850 --> 00:15:11,980
SIGN: Currently in 2nd
Keito Tachibana

477
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:08,760
KEITO: There's still a chance 
you can turn this around.

478
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:10,730
NATSUKI: Must be nice to be 
so calm in second place.

479
00:15:10,730 --> 00:15:12,940
KEITO: I wouldn't say I'm calm at all.

480
00:15:13,610 --> 00:15:14,530
KEITO: Oh?

481
00:15:14,530 --> 00:15:15,670
KEITO: Good morning, Tamon.

482
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:18,200
NATSUKI: What's up? It's rare for you to be late.

483
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,410
TAMON: Good... morning...

484
00:15:21,410 --> 00:15:22,660
THREE: Huh?

485
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:25,350
KEITO: Your voice is all raspy! What happened?!

486
00:15:26,590 --> 00:15:27,560
KEITO: Oh, Ouri.

487
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,580
KEITO: Morning.

488
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:31,840
OURI: Good morning...

489
00:15:32,450 --> 00:15:33,800
FOUR: Huh?!

490
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:41,050
SHIRAISHI: You'll all be singing 
the new song "RAIN" in full today.

491
00:15:41,430 --> 00:15:43,930
SHIRAISHI: I'm sure you've all 
practiced your hearts out.

492
00:15:43,930 --> 00:15:47,330
SHIRAISHI: Make sure you give it your all 
so you won't have any regrets.

493
00:15:48,230 --> 00:15:50,230
UTAGE/RIKO/YUINA: You've got this, Tamon-kun!

494
00:15:50,770 --> 00:15:54,690
SHIRAISHI: Let the final battle 
to determine the center begin!

495
00:15:57,610 --> 00:15:59,320
SIGN: Singing Expert

496
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:48,140
YUINA: Way to go, Tamon-kun! He definitely 
secured the center with that!

497
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,900
RIKO: Unlike the first round, 
it actually sounded

498
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:52,580
RIKO: like he was singing a ballad 
about heartbreak, didn't it?!

499
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:55,500
YUINA: Yeah! He did his best and was shining!

500
00:16:53,790 --> 00:16:56,730
UTAGE: It actually seemed like he was 
holding back his radiance...

501
00:16:56,730 --> 00:16:59,920
UTAGE: but it also seemed like 
he wasn't doing that well.

502
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:57,570
RIKO: He's never sung like that before, has he?

503
00:16:57,570 --> 00:16:59,260
YUINA: We saw another new side of Tamon!

504
00:16:59,260 --> 00:16:59,920
RIKO: Right?

505
00:17:02,430 --> 00:17:05,720
UTAGE: No! As Tamon-kun's fan, 
I need to believe in him!

506
00:17:06,490 --> 00:17:09,390
SHIRAISHI: All five episodes have 
concluded without issue.

507
00:17:09,390 --> 00:17:11,569
SHIRAISHI: The results are as I just told you.

508
00:17:12,319 --> 00:17:16,420
SHIRAISHI: The new song's pre-release at N Station's 
Summer Fes is just around the corner.

509
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:18,670
SHIRAISHI: I need you all to start practicing

510
00:17:18,670 --> 00:17:20,700
SHIRAISHI: the parts you've been assigned immediately.

511
00:17:21,569 --> 00:17:23,200
SHIRAISHI: Also...

512
00:17:24,339 --> 00:17:25,780
SHIRAISHI: Ouri, Tamon!

513
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:27,800
SHIRAISHI: What was that miserable display?!

514
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,730
SHIRAISHI: You might've fooled the viewers, 

515
00:17:29,730 --> 00:17:32,120
SHIRAISHI: but you can't deceive me or the judges!

516
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:35,380
SHIRAISHI: Are you really the same two that competed 
for first and second at the audition?

517
00:17:35,730 --> 00:17:38,960
SHIRAISHI: Practicing too much and overwork 
are both signs of failure!

518
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:40,990
SHIRAISHI: To become the best in the world, 

519
00:17:40,990 --> 00:17:44,330
SHIRAISHI: you need to perform 
at 2, 000% at any time!

520
00:17:45,970 --> 00:17:49,230
SHIRAISHI: F/ACE doesn't need any imperfections!

521
00:17:49,970 --> 00:17:52,310
YUINA: There's so much fan merch!

522
00:17:52,310 --> 00:17:54,230
RIKO: I'm gonna get this pink one.

523
00:17:53,810 --> 00:17:59,030
SIGN: Victory

524
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:57,060
YUINA: Hey look at this one. 
Obviously a must-buy.

525
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,690
UTAGE: Hm...

526
00:17:59,430 --> 00:18:03,490
UTAGE: The more I rewatch it, the more 
it looks like he wasn't doing very well.

527
00:18:03,490 --> 00:18:07,450
UTAGE: What am I going to do if Tamon-kun 
doesn't become the center?

528
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:12,160
UTAGE: I wonder how Gloomyhara-san's 
feeling right about now...

529
00:18:12,570 --> 00:18:14,920
UTAGE: I hope he's not all depressed from 
doomscrolling for his name.

530
00:18:15,270 --> 00:18:17,820
UTAGE: Have you been eating something 
other than cup noodles?

531
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:20,510
UTAGE: Have you been sleeping in your bed?

532
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:22,820
RIKO: Let's make a banner, too!

533
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:24,630
YUINA: We were allowed to bring those in, right?

534
00:18:24,630 --> 00:18:25,700
RIKO: Yeah, we can this time!

535
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:27,980
YUINA: Heck yeah! Now, then...

536
00:18:26,570 --> 00:18:30,460
UTAGE: You're not obsessing... 
and crying again, are you?

537
00:18:32,210 --> 00:18:36,730
UTAGE: I never worried like this 
before meeting Gloomyhara-san...

538
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:41,920
UTAGE: Am I... a failure as a fan?

539
00:18:58,450 --> 00:19:01,750
OURI: You usually just practice 
exactly as you're told to

540
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:03,970
OURI: without saying anything 
about how you feel...

541
00:19:03,970 --> 00:19:07,640
OURI: Yet you choose now to
 act up and self-destruct?

542
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:09,010
OURI: How stupid are you?

543
00:19:10,090 --> 00:19:14,270
TAMON: Yeah, but... you didn't do 
well this time either, Ouri-kun.

544
00:19:14,270 --> 00:19:18,360
OURI: Shut up! I always sorta choke 
when it counts!

545
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,900
OURI: I tried too hard and basically imploded.

546
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:22,400
OURI: Meaning, it's all your fault.

547
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,250
TAMON: What?

548
00:19:23,250 --> 00:19:25,190
OURI: And what happened to you?

549
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:28,660
TAMON: There are even more people 
supporting me now...

550
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:31,280
TAMON: and that made me happy.

551
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,670
TAMON: At the same time, I got 
overwhelmed with the feelings

552
00:19:34,670 --> 00:19:38,460
TAMON: of absolutely not wanting 
to fail or betray them.

553
00:19:40,570 --> 00:19:41,880
TAMON: It's weird.

554
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:45,520
TAMON: The more they're nice to me, 
the more happy and scared I become.

555
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:48,750
TAMON: I start to wonder what I'll do 
if I ever lose them...

556
00:19:48,750 --> 00:19:51,410
TAMON: and then I get scared again.

557
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:53,180
OURI: Gross.

558
00:19:54,270 --> 00:19:56,930
OURI: There are going to be 
some fans who drift away.

559
00:19:56,930 --> 00:19:59,290
OURI: And there'll be some fans who won't.

560
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:02,820
OURI: There's no point in thinking 
about something so obvious.

561
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:04,320
OURI: I just don't get it.

562
00:20:05,890 --> 00:20:08,520
TAMON: I thought I understood that in my head...

563
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,660
TAMON: But maybe I just thought I understood.

564
00:20:12,190 --> 00:20:14,930
TAMON: All those kind words and yet...

565
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:21,250
TAMON: What the heck am I even doing?

566
00:20:22,450 --> 00:20:26,050
OURI: How long are you gonna dwell 
on what happened in the past?

567
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:41,850
SIGN: Tamon FTW

568
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:41,850
SIGN: Tamon FTW

